<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard II of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1367">1367</a>–<a href="/years/1400">1400</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Richard II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1377 to 1399, succeeding his grandfather Edward III at the age of ten. As a boy of fourteen he faced the rebels of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a> in 1381. His later reign was marked by conflict with the great nobles, several of whom he struck down in 1397, and in 1399 his exiled cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england">Henry Bolingbroke</a> returned, deposed him and took the throne as Henry IV. Richard died in captivity at Pontefract Castle early in 1400.</p></div>
